  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mover></math>Hydration energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8593;</mo></math></p><p>As the size of gaseous ion decreases, it gets more hydrated in water and hence, the size of aqueous ion increases. When this bulky ion move in solution, it experience greater resistance and hence lower conductivity.</p><p>Size of gaseous ion:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>Size of aqueous ion:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>Conductivity:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p>",
